{"title":"Leonhard Kestel","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Leonhard Kestel","image":"img/profile.png","image-alt":"Profile picture of Leonhard Kestel","about":{"template":"trestles","links":[{"text":"GitHub","icon":"github","url":"https://github.com/kestelnadomu"},{"text":"ORCID","icon":"person-circle","url":"https://orcid.org/0009-0008-4549-4960"},{"text":"Scholar","icon":"journal","url":"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=VQ63JF0AAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao"},{"text":"Email","icon":"envelope","url":"mailto:leo.kestel@lmu.de"}]},"comments":false},"headingText":"About","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n::: {.column-page}\n\nI am a PhD candidate at the *Social Data Science and AI* Lab, which is part of the Statistics Department of the Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität in Munich. \n\nWith a background in Psychology and Computer Science, I am a native to interdisciplinary research with focus on the application of Machine Learning algorithms in social sciences and the public sector.\n  \nIn my research\n<!-- - for which I received a scholarship from the Bavarian Institute for Digital Transformation (*bidt*) -  -->\nI try to use Neurosymbolic architectures as an interface to incorporate arbitrary ethical constraints, formalized in logic or as causal graphs, into the machine learning process.\n\nI am a member of the *ADA* initiative and a co-founder of *ondatix Datenwerkstatt GmbH*, which both aim to support the public administration with data scientific expertise and tools. Therefore, we organise workshops and develop applications for public servants.\n\n<!-- **Keywords:** Neurosymbolic AI, Algorithmic Fairness, Trustworthy ML -->\n\n\n## Affiliations\n[<img class=\"soda\" alt=\"SODA\">](https://www.stat.lmu.de/soda)\n[<img class=\"lmu\" alt=\"LMU\">](https://www.lmu.de)\n[<img class=\"mcml\" alt=\"MCML\">](https://www.mcml.ai)\n[<img class=\"bidt\" alt=\"bidt\">](https://www.bidt.digital)\n[<img class=\"ada\" alt=\"ADA\">](https://www.ada-oeffentliche-verwaltung.de)\n<!-- [<img class=\"ondatix\" alt=\"ondatix\">](https://www.ondatix.org) -->\n\n\n:::\n\n\n\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n::: {.column-page}\n\n## About\nI am a PhD candidate at the *Social Data Science and AI* Lab, which is part of the Statistics Department of the Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität in Munich. \n\nWith a background in Psychology and Computer Science, I am a native to interdisciplinary research with focus on the application of Machine Learning algorithms in social sciences and the public sector.\n  \nIn my research\n<!-- - for which I received a scholarship from the Bavarian Institute for Digital Transformation (*bidt*) -  -->\nI try to use Neurosymbolic architectures as an interface to incorporate arbitrary ethical constraints, formalized in logic or as causal graphs, into the machine learning process.\n\nI am a member of the *ADA* initiative and a co-founder of *ondatix Datenwerkstatt GmbH*, which both aim to support the public administration with data scientific expertise and tools. Therefore, we organise workshops and develop applications for public servants.\n\n<!-- **Keywords:** Neurosymbolic AI, Algorithmic Fairness, Trustworthy ML -->\n\n\n## Affiliations\n[<img class=\"soda\" alt=\"SODA\">](https://www.stat.lmu.de/soda)\n[<img class=\"lmu\" alt=\"LMU\">](https://www.lmu.de)\n[<img class=\"mcml\" alt=\"MCML\">](https://www.mcml.ai)\n[<img class=\"bidt\" alt=\"bidt\">](https://www.bidt.digital)\n[<img class=\"ada\" alt=\"ADA\">](https://www.ada-oeffentliche-verwaltung.de)\n<!-- [<img class=\"ondatix\" alt=\"ondatix\">](https://www.ondatix.org) -->\n\n\n:::\n\n\n\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":"auto","echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart"